# The intervals the suites keep on purpose, one per line as FILE: REASON,
# in the words of the `interval:` mark on the line; tools/verify/suitecheck.sh
# refuses a sleep without one. A person reads this list.
tests/system/suites.mk: the machine is asked every second until init has started SSH
tests/system/suites.mk: the service log is read every second until the client gives up
tests/system/suites/bootline.sh: the machine runs on after the line to show it stopped there
tests/system/suites/diskdiag.sh: a try of SSH every two seconds until the server answers
tests/system/suites/doom.sh: doom runs for ten seconds; the row counts its disk commands
tests/system/suites/drill.sh: the service log is read every second for recovery's fixed address
tests/system/suites/drill.sh: the service log is read every three seconds for the lease
tests/system/suites/gnu.sh: a try of SSH every two seconds until the server answers
tests/system/suites/grow.sh: the resizer is killed after its period; the row proves the repair
tests/system/suites/make.sh: the file's time must pass the second, which make compares whole
tests/system/suites/metal.sh: a try of SSH every two seconds until the server answers
tests/system/suites/mount.sh: a sleeper holds the file open across the umount that must fail
tests/system/suites/procfiles.sh: the guest's table is read every second for the host's connection
tests/system/suites/sealed.sh: a try of SSH every two seconds until the server answers
tests/system/suites/selfbuild.sh: the self-built server is asked every second until it answers
tests/system/suites/servicelog.sh: the guest polls the log's size each second until init bounds it
tests/system/suites/ssh.sh: a holder keeps a flood writer open until the flood is killed
tests/system/suites/ssh.sh: the forty connections are counted once the guest has taken them
tests/system/suites/ssh.sh: the next reading of a count that only the guest advances
tests/system/suites/ssh.sh: the next reading, while the released connections close
tests/system/suites/drill.sh: a holder keeps the console's feed open while the machine runs
tests/system/suites/grub.sh: a holder keeps the console's feed open while the machine runs
tests/system/suites/install.sh: a holder keeps the console's feed open while the machine runs
tests/system/suites/menu.sh: a holder keeps the console's feed open while the machine runs
tests/system/suites/metal.sh: a reset before the session is tried again after a second
tests/system/accept/metal_accept.sh: a reset before the session is tried again after a second
